Hmm. Looks like I'm going to have to graduate to 3.0. I've never had
boots -- don't know if they exist in 2.3, and I've p-morphed armor
until the wands ran out looking for helmets and gloves, but still
never gotten boots. Xans are easy to kill, but they tend to get that
first hit.

Umber hulks in 2.3 don't tunnel (or I've never seen one do it, at
least), and there are no unicorn horns. They're not usually much
problem, but I've gotten confused by them at critical times. Related
question: someone else mentioned that they let umber hulks confuse
them so that they can get confused spell effects. I thought that for
some reason you only got those effects when confused by a potion, and
not by a wand or a monster. Seems like a silly restriction, but I
thought that's the way it was.

Nymphs are a *major* pain. Cancellation makes them "plain" so that
they can't seduce, but they still steal. And they move too darn fast.
More importantly, there's no benefit from them. Other things, like
Vampires and Dragons (we're still talking 2.3 here, so there aren't
any grades of these), are a pain, but it's worth having them alive for
other reasons.

Nurses, again, are a nuisance. There's no way in hell :-) I'm going to
take off my armor and weapon, and I don't like killing the other human
monsters. No luckstones and no sacrificing.

Anyway, I've just moved to a system with 2MB RAM, so I can finally
build 3.0, and find out about all this other neat stuff people are
talking about.
